WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.090
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.360 --> 01:34.940
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.330 --> 01:37.890
[Episode 2]

4
01:38.640 --> 01:42.020
The Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army grew from the Nanchang,

5
01:42.020 --> 01:44.300
Autumn Harvest, and Guangzhou Uprisings

6
01:43.170 --> 01:44.140
[Zhu De, Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,]

7
01:44.140 --> 01:45.110
[Commander-in-Chief of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

8
01:44.630 --> 01:47.030
to dozens of uprisings across the country,

9
01:47.280 --> 01:48.729
established more than a dozen revolutionary base areas,

10
01:48.729 --> 01:52.140
from Jinggangshan to other parts of the country,

11
01:52.400 --> 01:55.120
and thwarted several enemy encirclement campaigns.

12
01:55.120 --> 01:56.320
Over the past 7 years,

13
01:56.350 --> 01:59.789
we forged an army of iron!

14
02:00.710 --> 02:04.680
Yet many of our brave comrades

15
02:01.570 --> 02:04.750
[Bo Gu (Qin Bangxian), Head of the CPC Central Committee]

16
02:04.760 --> 02:05.950
[Xiang Ying, Secretary of the Secretariat of the CPC Central Committee,]

17
02:04.760 --> 02:08.800
fell under the enemy's hail of bullets and artillery fire.

18
02:05.950 --> 02:07.150
[Vice Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

19
02:07.150 --> 02:08.289
[Mao Zedong, Chairman of the Central Executive Committee]

20
02:08.289 --> 02:09.440
[and Chairman of the Council of People's Commissars of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

21
02:09.180 --> 02:11.580
We should not forget them,

22
02:09.440 --> 02:09.870
[Zhou Enlai, Member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee,]

23
02:09.870 --> 02:10.310
[Vice Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,]

24
02:10.310 --> 02:11.190
[and Political Commissar-General of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

25
02:11.190 --> 02:12.170
[Wang Jiaxiang, Vice Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,]

26
02:11.780 --> 02:13.260
and we will never forget them!

27
02:12.170 --> 02:13.150
[Director of the General Political Department of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

28
02:13.150 --> 02:13.860
[Luofu (Zhang Wentian),]

29
02:13.860 --> 02:14.570
[Member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee]

30
02:13.920 --> 02:14.640
Comrades.

31
02:14.570 --> 02:16.900
[Li Zhuoran, Director of the Political Department of the 1st Red Army Corps]

32
02:15.000 --> 02:16.750
Did you hear any sounds?

33
02:17.670 --> 02:20.350
I think you must have heard

34
02:20.540 --> 02:24.630
the singing, laughter, and slogans here.

35
02:25.200 --> 02:27.550
But as a veteran,

36
02:28.150 --> 02:32.020
I could hear the enemy's horses circling the Soviet Area,

37
02:32.180 --> 02:33.890
the sound of barbed wire being dragged,

38
02:33.890 --> 02:36.360
the clang of hammers pounding stakes into the ground!

39
02:36.360 --> 02:39.730
I could hear the gunfire, artillery, and battle cries

40
02:39.780 --> 02:43.620
coming from the front lines at Jianning and Guangchang!

41
02:41.470 --> 02:42.480
[Qian Zhuangfei, Deputy Director of the Second Bureau]

42
02:42.480 --> 02:43.490
[of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

43
02:44.090 --> 02:47.250
Comrades, the enemy is closing in!

44
02:45.829 --> 02:48.050
[Liu Ying, Director of the Propaganda Department of the Central Committee]

45
02:47.590 --> 02:50.560
A brutal battle lies ahead!

46
02:48.050 --> 02:50.280
[of the Young Communist League of China]

47
02:51.630 --> 02:52.430
This tower

48
02:53.600 --> 02:56.440
is not only a monument to our fallen heroes,

49
02:57.120 --> 02:58.450
but also a beacon.

50
02:59.470 --> 03:01.280
The spirit

51
03:01.590 --> 03:02.920
of every fallen comrade

52
03:02.920 --> 03:05.690
will become a ray of light,

53
03:06.150 --> 03:07.210
shining down on us,

54
03:07.470 --> 03:08.520
guiding us,

55
03:08.810 --> 03:09.860
inspiring us!

56
03:10.550 --> 03:14.230
Our fallen comrades will remind us

57
03:14.770 --> 03:16.840
that no matter how powerful the enemy,

58
03:16.840 --> 03:19.360
no matter how devastating the sacrifices,

59
03:19.680 --> 03:22.240
nothing can shake or destroy

60
03:22.260 --> 03:23.670
the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army's

61
03:23.670 --> 03:26.020
ironclad fighting spirit

62
03:26.310 --> 03:29.470
or its rock-solid revolutionary faith.

63
03:26.360 --> 03:27.460
[Liu Caixiang, Director of the Women's Department]

64
03:27.460 --> 03:28.560
[of the Guangdong-Jiangxi Provincial Committee of the CPC]

65
03:29.840 --> 03:33.240
Let us follow in the bloodstained footsteps of our fallen heroes.

66
03:33.240 --> 03:36.200
Victory will surely be ours!

67
03:36.670 --> 03:38.860
Long live the Communist Party of China!

68
03:38.860 --> 03:41.310
Long live the Communist Party of China!

69
03:41.329 --> 03:42.770
Long live the Soviets!

70
03:43.120 --> 03:44.590
Long live the Soviets!

71
03:45.079 --> 03:46.340
Long live the Red Army!

72
03:46.520 --> 03:48.680
Long live the Red Army!

73
03:48.840 --> 03:50.590
Long live the Communist Party of China!

74
03:50.590 --> 03:52.750
Long live the Communist Party of China!

75
03:52.750 --> 03:54.310
Long live the Soviets!

76
03:54.310 --> 03:56.310
Long live the Soviets!

77
03:56.310 --> 03:57.710
Long live the Red Army!

78
03:57.710 --> 03:59.400
Long live the Red Army!

79
03:59.520 --> 04:01.470
Long live the Communist Party of China!

80
04:01.470 --> 04:03.800
Long live the Communist Party of China!

81
04:04.400 --> 04:05.590
Long live the Soviets!

82
04:05.590 --> 04:07.120
Long live the Soviets!

83
04:07.240 --> 04:08.710
Long live the Red Army!

84
04:08.800 --> 04:10.630
Long live the Red Army!

85
04:48.840 --> 04:53.430
[Guangchang, Jiangxi]

86
04:49.360 --> 04:51.750
On April 10, 1934,

87
04:52.840 --> 04:54.159
the Nationalist encirclement forces

88
04:54.159 --> 04:56.560
advanced on Guangchang, the northern gateway to the Central Soviet Area,

89
04:56.560 --> 04:58.510
along two routes.

90
05:00.160 --> 05:01.720
Bo Gu and Li De

91
05:01.800 --> 05:02.800
went to the front

92
05:02.800 --> 05:05.750
to establish a field headquarters and direct the defense.

93
05:05.750 --> 05:09.480
They continued to adhere to conservative strategies and tactics.

94
05:10.490 --> 05:12.690
More than 20,000 Red Army soldiers

95
05:12.720 --> 05:15.180
fought fierce battles against the Nationalist forces

96
05:15.180 --> 05:17.710
across an open stretch of land spanning 20 km.

97
05:19.310 --> 05:21.190
Under the enemy's overwhelming

98
05:21.210 --> 05:23.010
heavy firepower,

99
05:23.350 --> 05:26.440
the Red Army suffered massive casualties.

100
05:27.480 --> 05:28.880
Just look at this! Look!

101
05:27.520 --> 05:34.520
[Mount Daluo, Guangchang, Jiangxi, Headquarters of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

102
05:28.920 --> 05:30.970
If that foreign adviser had used his head,

103
05:30.970 --> 05:33.560
he'd never have made us fight a positional battle at Guangchang!

104
05:33.560 --> 05:34.830
We've submitted several reports already,

105
05:34.830 --> 05:36.100
but there's been no response.

106
05:36.100 --> 05:37.470
Peng, calm down.

107
05:37.870 --> 05:39.070
I'm the commander-in-chief,

108
05:39.070 --> 05:41.600
yet I can't even command a single machine gun!

109
05:44.480 --> 05:49.750
[Peng Dehuai, Commander of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

110
05:46.480 --> 05:48.080
And what about our soldiers?

111
05:48.310 --> 05:51.310
They're dying on the battlefield for nothing!

112
05:51.730 --> 05:52.610
Reporting in!

113
05:53.240 --> 05:55.240
This is the battle plan

114
05:55.240 --> 05:56.550
Comrade Li De has sent you.

115
05:56.550 --> 05:58.750
Please carry it out as soon as possible.

116
06:01.390 --> 06:03.000
Didn't our chief of staff, Deng Ping,

117
06:03.000 --> 06:03.830
already submit

118
06:03.830 --> 06:05.430
our own battle plan?

119
06:05.680 --> 06:06.880
Comrade Li De said...

120
06:07.010 --> 06:07.770
He said

121
06:08.220 --> 06:10.950
Chief of Staff Deng's plan was full of flaws.

122
06:11.720 --> 06:13.560
He also said...

123
06:13.900 --> 06:16.660
[Yang Shangkun, Political Commissar of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

124
06:14.120 --> 06:14.980
He also said...

125
06:15.860 --> 06:16.990
What else did he say?

126
06:17.480 --> 06:18.310
He also said

127
06:18.720 --> 06:21.780
Chief of Staff Deng wasted his time at military school.

128
06:21.890 --> 06:23.330
This is ridiculous!

129
06:23.620 --> 06:25.320
It's all right, Peng. Don't get worked up.

130
06:25.320 --> 06:27.350
Go tell that foreign adviser

131
06:27.370 --> 06:31.670
[Deng Ping, Chief of Staff of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

132
06:27.780 --> 06:29.540
that Chief of Staff Deng Ping

133
06:29.960 --> 06:31.890
has fought alongside us for years.

134
06:32.110 --> 06:34.570
We've commanded hundreds of battles together.

135
06:34.570 --> 06:35.810
His military prowess

136
06:36.240 --> 06:38.240
has been proven on the battlefield!

137
06:38.420 --> 06:40.540
Also, that foreign adviser

138
06:40.730 --> 06:43.090
marked a machine-gun position on the map,

139
06:43.430 --> 06:44.340
but in reality,

140
06:44.870 --> 06:46.330
there's a huge pond there.

141
06:46.610 --> 06:47.650
Go ask him

142
06:47.720 --> 06:50.780
how we're supposed to set up machine guns over the pond!

143
06:52.550 --> 06:53.380
Go on.

144
06:55.190 --> 06:56.790
Tell him exactly what I said!

145
06:56.980 --> 06:57.690
Easy.

146
07:04.920 --> 07:06.510
Hang in there, comrade.

147
07:06.510 --> 07:08.310
Get me the gauze, quick!

148
07:12.720 --> 07:13.800
Hang in there! Hang in there!

149
07:13.800 --> 07:14.600
Hang in there!

150
07:21.680 --> 07:27.330
[Ganzhu, Guangchang, Jiangxi, Positions of the 4th Regiment]

151
07:50.860 --> 07:54.130
Comrades, hold the line at all costs!

152
07:51.580 --> 07:53.990
[Geng Biao, Commander of the 4th Regiment, 2nd Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

153
07:54.050 --> 07:56.360
[Mao Zhenhua, Company Commander of the 3rd Company, 1st Battalion, 4th Regiment]

154
08:12.270 --> 08:14.400
Get the ammunition to the 3rd Company!

155
08:18.000 --> 08:18.910
[Yang Chengwu, Political Commissar]

156
08:18.910 --> 08:19.830
[of the 4th Regiment, 2nd Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

157
08:37.750 --> 08:39.669
Mao Zhenhua, move up!

158
08:39.789 --> 08:41.200
Reinforce the 1st Company!

159
08:41.200 --> 08:42.000
Yes, sir!

160
08:42.039 --> 08:44.280
3rd Company, move out!

161
09:01.320 --> 09:03.320
Huang Xiaolin, hang in there!

162
09:03.550 --> 09:05.510
Keep collecting ammunition!

163
09:08.320 --> 09:09.120
Fire!

164
09:32.440 --> 09:35.340
[Ganzhu, Guangchang, Jiangxi]

165
09:33.770 --> 09:34.410
Hold on!

166
09:35.340 --> 09:38.240
[Headquarters of the 1st Red Army Corps]

167
09:38.840 --> 09:39.500
Be careful.

168
09:39.790 --> 09:41.250
Coming through! Make way!

169
09:45.960 --> 09:47.220
Comrade, bear with it.

170
09:56.990 --> 09:58.050
Make way! Make way!

171
10:00.220 --> 10:01.550
Medic, over here!

172
10:07.910 --> 10:09.600
It's all right. Hang in there!

173
10:09.600 --> 10:10.200
Over here!

174
10:16.710 --> 10:18.310
Just hold on a little longer.

175
10:19.410 --> 10:21.010
Our casualties are too high.

176
10:21.680 --> 10:22.630
Chief of Staff,

177
10:22.920 --> 10:25.520
has the field headquarters issued any orders?

178
10:25.540 --> 10:26.260
No.

179
10:28.580 --> 10:32.050
[Lin Biao, Commander of the 1st Red Army Corps]

180
10:28.740 --> 10:30.780
Send a telegram to the field headquarters.

181
10:30.780 --> 10:32.200
If we're determined to keep fighting,

182
10:32.200 --> 10:34.260
we should abandon the outer defensive positions

183
10:34.260 --> 10:35.690
and pull our troops outside Guangchang.

184
10:35.590 --> 10:38.360
[Nie Rongzhen, Political Commissar of the 1st Red Army Corps]

185
10:36.360 --> 10:38.490
Otherwise, we'll lose all our fighting strength

186
10:38.490 --> 10:40.380
[Zuo Quan, Chief of Staff of the 1st Red Army Corps]

187
10:38.960 --> 10:41.220
before the decisive battle even begins.

188
10:41.960 --> 10:43.320
Send it exactly like that.

189
10:43.320 --> 10:44.010
Watch out!

190
11:31.870 --> 11:40.090
♪ Little stars, little stars, fill the sky ♪

191
11:41.350 --> 11:50.180
♪ Fly to the west bank of Yongxin River ♪

192
11:51.290 --> 11:55.380
♪ One to the east ♪

193
11:55.640 --> 11:59.870
♪ One to the west ♪

194
12:00.530 --> 12:09.350
♪ Count and count, there's no end in sight ♪

195
12:10.370 --> 12:22.630
♪ Little stars hide and play peekaboo with me ♪

196
12:58.560 --> 13:01.370
[Temple of Sanguan, Guangchang, Jiangxi]

197
12:58.960 --> 13:00.200
Comrade Li De,

198
13:00.360 --> 13:01.670
please reconsider

199
13:01.370 --> 13:04.190
[Red Army Field Headquarters]

200
13:01.790 --> 13:03.940
Comrades Peng Dehuai and Lin Biao's opinions.

201
13:03.940 --> 13:05.510
Given the current situation,

202
13:05.510 --> 13:07.440
we shouldn't make a new battle plan.

203
13:07.440 --> 13:08.630
Does the new battle plan

204
13:08.630 --> 13:09.550
call for abandoning Guangchang?

205
13:09.550 --> 13:10.240
Does the new battle plan

206
13:10.240 --> 13:11.270
call for abandoning Guangchang?

207
13:11.270 --> 13:13.390
Comrade Bocheng, as Chief of the General Staff,

208
13:13.390 --> 13:15.970
you should help improve Comrade Li De's battle plan,

209
13:15.970 --> 13:17.240
not undermine his

210
13:17.240 --> 13:18.640
determination to fight!

211
13:18.880 --> 13:21.280
The troops at the front are suffering terribly.

212
13:21.280 --> 13:23.680
We can't keep wasting our forces like this.

213
13:25.170 --> 13:26.660
Comrades,

214
13:25.930 --> 13:28.530
[Li De (Otto Braun), Military Adviser from the Communist International]

215
13:27.240 --> 13:28.960
let me make this clear once again.

216
13:28.960 --> 13:31.200
Comrade Li De is a military adviser

217
13:31.200 --> 13:33.070
sent to us by the Communist International.

218
13:33.070 --> 13:35.600
His command is based on the Soviet Union's successful experience.

219
13:35.600 --> 13:36.440
Move faster!

220
13:36.750 --> 13:37.510
Follow me!

221
13:37.510 --> 13:38.680
Comrades, pick up the pace!

222
13:38.680 --> 13:40.960
Guangchang is our Madrid.

223
13:41.530 --> 13:42.730
If we can't hold Guangchang,

224
13:42.730 --> 13:44.640
we'll have no way to answer to the Communist International.

225
13:44.640 --> 13:46.450
No one can bear the political responsibility.

226
13:46.450 --> 13:48.410
We'll have no way to answer to the Communist International.

227
13:48.410 --> 13:51.010
No one can bear the political responsibility.

228
14:02.360 --> 14:03.850
♪ Red-stemmed tree ♪

229
14:04.030 --> 14:05.360
♪ Red-stemmed flowers ♪

230
14:05.740 --> 14:08.580
♪ White flowers bloom on the red-stemmed tree ♪

231
14:09.150 --> 14:11.510
♪ White flowers bear black seeds ♪

232
14:11.800 --> 14:13.750
♪ Black seeds fall into someone's home ♪

233
14:21.410 --> 14:24.350
[Shazhouba, Ruijin, Jiangxi]

234
14:21.870 --> 14:23.120
Roger. Roger.

235
14:24.350 --> 14:27.300
[Office of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

236
14:25.770 --> 14:27.570
Vice Chairman Zhou, a telegram.

237
14:30.320 --> 14:31.150
Here, here.

238
14:40.620 --> 14:41.390
Reporting in!

239
14:41.390 --> 14:44.450
Vice Chairman Zhou, an urgent telegram from the front.

240
15:23.390 --> 15:26.190
Vice Chairman Zhou, an urgent call from the front.

241
15:28.720 --> 15:29.130
Hello?

242
15:29.730 --> 15:30.330
Speaking.

243
15:32.230 --> 15:33.630
All right, I understand.

244
15:33.760 --> 15:35.200
Report any new developments

245
15:35.200 --> 15:36.260
to me immediately.

246
15:37.610 --> 15:40.340
Reporting in! An urgent telegram from the front!

247
15:53.360 --> 15:54.290
Comrade Zedong?

248
15:56.120 --> 15:56.640
Enlai.

249
15:57.640 --> 15:58.840
When did you get here?

250
15:59.250 --> 15:59.920
Just now.

251
16:00.510 --> 16:01.110
Come on in.

252
16:05.340 --> 16:07.340
You're busy with military affairs.

253
16:07.700 --> 16:09.530
The situation in Guangchang is extremely critical.

254
16:09.530 --> 16:11.910
The enemy keeps pushing back our outer defenses.

255
16:11.910 --> 16:13.370
Our troops have suffered heavy casualties.

256
16:13.370 --> 16:15.230
There's nowhere left to retreat.

257
16:18.250 --> 16:20.910
Are they still insisting on holding the ground?

258
16:23.750 --> 16:25.200
In the name of the CPC Central Committee,

259
16:25.200 --> 16:27.650
the Central Revolutionary Military Commission, and the Red Army General Political Department,

260
16:27.650 --> 16:28.200
they've just issued

261
16:28.200 --> 16:30.290
the Political Order to Defend Guangchang.

262
16:30.290 --> 16:32.670
It demands that our troops stand firm without wavering

263
16:32.670 --> 16:35.730
and launch counterattacks under enemy artillery fire

264
16:35.770 --> 16:37.170
and aerial bombardment.

265
16:45.970 --> 16:47.700
Did you need something from me?

266
16:47.880 --> 16:49.610
I came to report my plans to you.

267
16:49.940 --> 16:51.030
You could say I'm here to say goodbye, too.

268
16:51.030 --> 16:52.160
Where are you going?

269
16:53.280 --> 16:53.880
Huichang.

270
16:54.670 --> 16:57.600
I'm going to Huichang to investigate the situation.

271
17:01.610 --> 17:02.860
You've got a tough job ahead.

272
17:02.860 --> 17:05.540
I'll do what I can.

273
17:08.990 --> 17:09.920
Comrade Zedong.

274
17:14.869 --> 17:17.740
Looking back, many of your ideas

275
17:17.760 --> 17:19.359
were far ahead of their time.

276
17:19.790 --> 17:20.700
Tell me,

277
17:21.400 --> 17:24.960
do we still have a chance to take the fight beyond our lines?

278
17:26.670 --> 17:27.930
As long as we're alive,

279
17:29.160 --> 17:30.440
anything is possible.

280
17:31.030 --> 17:31.950
If we're dead,

281
17:32.350 --> 17:33.590
what's the point

282
17:33.920 --> 17:35.140
of holding Guangchang?

283
17:35.140 --> 17:37.400
We'd lose both our men and our territory.

284
17:40.130 --> 17:41.130
I understand.

285
17:41.920 --> 17:43.320
When you get to Huichang,

286
17:43.720 --> 17:46.180
write to me if you come up with any good ideas.

287
17:46.660 --> 17:48.900
All right. Get back to it.

288
17:58.640 --> 18:01.030
On April 28, 1934,

289
18:02.310 --> 18:04.790
the Battle of Guangchang, which lasted 18 days,

290
18:04.790 --> 18:07.200
ended with the Central Red Army in full retreat

291
18:07.200 --> 18:09.850
and the enemy occupying Guangchang.

292
18:09.630 --> 18:16.910
[Toubei Town, Guangchang, Jiangxi; Feng Family Ancestral Hall]

293
18:10.320 --> 18:13.930
Every one of your corps

294
18:15.450 --> 18:18.800
was defeated in positional warfare focused on defense.

295
18:18.830 --> 18:20.960
These were decisions made by your staff.

296
18:20.960 --> 18:23.200
You didn't carry out an effective defensive operation

297
18:23.200 --> 18:24.640
as I instructed.

298
18:25.070 --> 18:27.920
Your commanders have completely failed

299
18:27.920 --> 18:32.680
to grasp the essence of the short, sharp attack tactic.

300
18:32.700 --> 18:34.460
That's our biggest problem.

301
18:39.590 --> 18:42.510
I'd like to say a few words.

302
18:50.750 --> 18:51.510
Li De,

303
18:52.090 --> 18:53.350
all you ever talk about

304
18:54.050 --> 18:56.580
is conventional warfare, fortress warfare,

305
18:56.930 --> 18:58.220
and "short, sharp attacks."

306
18:58.220 --> 18:59.620
Fine. Let me ask you this.

307
18:59.990 --> 19:01.720
How can we attack without ammunition?

308
19:01.720 --> 19:03.980
How can we attack without heavy weapons?

309
19:04.170 --> 19:05.300
Our soldiers are now

310
19:05.420 --> 19:06.550
risking their lives

311
19:07.050 --> 19:09.250
in a war of attrition against the enemy.

312
19:09.830 --> 19:11.030
They're human lives!

313
19:11.270 --> 19:12.470
How many more can we afford to lose?

314
19:12.470 --> 19:15.070
Why don't you bring planes, artillery, and tanks

315
19:15.070 --> 19:17.200
to China and fight a conventional war?

316
19:17.950 --> 19:18.980
[Wu Xiuquan, Translator]

317
19:18.220 --> 19:19.340
Comrade Peng Dehuai.

318
19:19.340 --> 19:20.440
Stick to the facts.

319
19:21.160 --> 19:22.820
Leave your emotions out of it.

320
19:25.200 --> 19:26.130
Wu Xiuquan,

321
19:27.110 --> 19:30.040
don't leave out a single word. Translate for him.

322
19:31.090 --> 19:31.720
All right.

323
19:33.550 --> 19:36.680
He says all you talk about is conventional warfare and fortress warfare.

324
19:36.680 --> 19:37.640
He asks,

325
19:37.700 --> 19:40.430
how can we repel an attack without heavy weapons?

326
19:40.550 --> 19:42.680
Our soldiers keep making sacrifices.

327
19:43.110 --> 19:45.070
Why don't you bring planes, tanks, and artillery

328
19:45.070 --> 19:47.590
from the Soviet Union

329
19:47.960 --> 19:49.070
to China?

330
19:51.880 --> 19:52.800
Peng Dehuai,

331
19:53.210 --> 19:56.780
do you think I traveled halfway around the world to China

332
19:57.440 --> 19:58.440
just to sabotage your efforts?

333
19:58.440 --> 19:59.720
Do you think I traveled halfway around the world to China...

334
19:59.720 --> 20:01.270
Peng, that's enough.

335
20:01.300 --> 20:02.300
I have more to say.

336
20:02.410 --> 20:04.780
Li De, how many times have I warned you?

337
20:05.080 --> 20:05.990
Your command

338
20:06.010 --> 20:07.140
has cost our Red Army

339
20:07.150 --> 20:10.000
its advantage in mobility, flexibility, and concentrated attacks.

340
20:10.000 --> 20:10.880
At best, you're just

341
20:10.880 --> 20:12.720
a tactician who fights on paper.

342
20:12.950 --> 20:13.970
In China, there's an idiom

343
20:13.970 --> 20:15.410
for what you're doing:

344
20:15.760 --> 20:17.160
armchair strategizing.

345
20:19.120 --> 20:20.290
Our Red Army

346
20:20.710 --> 20:23.370
has fought in Fujian and Jiangxi for 7 or 8 years.

347
20:23.830 --> 20:26.480
It took us years of hard fighting to secure this base area.

348
20:26.480 --> 20:27.480
But look at us now.

349
20:27.600 --> 20:29.420
Our forces are dwindling with every battle!

350
20:29.420 --> 20:30.690
In the Battle of Guangchang,

351
20:30.690 --> 20:31.970
our 3rd Red Army Corps alone

352
20:31.970 --> 20:37.380
lost 2,705 men!

353
20:37.560 --> 20:40.480
You're so careless with what's not yours to lose!

354
20:41.310 --> 20:42.070
Enough!

355
21:01.880 --> 21:04.080
Shangkun, translate that.

356
21:09.960 --> 21:13.270
You're so careless with what's not yours to lose.

357
21:13.670 --> 21:15.080
You've gone too far.

358
21:15.810 --> 21:17.240
Peng Dehuai.

359
21:17.650 --> 21:19.740
Peng Dehuai, you've gone too far.

360
21:21.140 --> 21:24.730
I know why you're acting this way.

361
21:25.440 --> 21:26.960
You're upset that you were removed

362
21:26.960 --> 21:30.300
as Vice Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,

363
21:30.300 --> 21:31.260
aren't you?

364
21:31.660 --> 21:33.590
You're upset that you were removed

365
21:33.640 --> 21:36.470
as Vice Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission.

366
21:36.470 --> 21:38.000
That's a petty way to think.

367
21:38.330 --> 21:41.530
I have never cared about holding office.

368
21:42.440 --> 21:44.170
All I want is to lead my soldiers

369
21:46.120 --> 21:47.640
to victory!

370
21:48.720 --> 21:50.270
All I want is victory.

371
21:59.150 --> 22:00.550
I've brought my luggage.

372
22:01.090 --> 22:02.820
I'll go back to Ruijin with you.

373
22:03.220 --> 22:04.620
Whether it's dismissal,

374
22:04.670 --> 22:05.530
a public trial,

375
22:06.080 --> 22:06.880
or execution,

376
22:08.230 --> 22:09.430
I have no objections.

377
22:11.470 --> 22:12.840
I have no objections.

378
22:31.080 --> 22:31.550
[Li Zhuoran, Director of the Political Department of the 1st Red Army Corps]

379
22:31.550 --> 22:32.030
[Dong Zhentang, Commander of the 5th Red Army Corps]

380
22:32.030 --> 22:32.990
[Cai Shufan, Political Commissar of the 9th Red Army Corps]

381
22:44.070 --> 22:45.400
After Guangchang fell,

382
22:45.880 --> 22:49.750
the Nationalist army launched a full-scale offensive

383
22:49.780 --> 22:51.550
from the north, east, and south,

384
22:51.550 --> 22:54.440
advancing toward the heart of the Central Soviet Area.

385
22:54.440 --> 22:56.870
The Red Army suffered heavy losses,

386
22:57.090 --> 22:59.200
and positions kept falling.

387
22:57.820 --> 23:03.100
[Ruijin]

388
22:59.630 --> 23:02.960
It had become extremely difficult to fight on interior lines.

389
23:02.960 --> 23:04.200
In the Central Soviet Area,

390
23:04.200 --> 23:06.000
breaking the enemy's encirclement campaigns

391
23:06.000 --> 23:07.530
was now all but impossible.

392
23:09.800 --> 23:15.290
[Shazhouba, Ruijin, Jiangxi; Office of the CPC Central Committee]

393
23:23.170 --> 23:28.540
Are we here to hold a meeting or sit in silence?

394
23:28.840 --> 23:31.000
You can speak up if you have any concerns.

395
23:31.000 --> 23:34.330
Fine. Then let's discuss

396
23:32.290 --> 23:34.220
[Luofu (Zhang Wentian), Member of the Standing Committee]

397
23:34.220 --> 23:36.160
[of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee]

398
23:35.090 --> 23:38.240
the serious errors in command

399
23:38.520 --> 23:41.520
during the Battle of Guangchang.

400
23:41.760 --> 23:42.620
In that battle,

401
23:42.640 --> 23:45.920
we killed, wounded, or captured over 2,600 enemy soldiers.

402
23:45.920 --> 23:47.470
Our own casualties

403
23:48.880 --> 23:50.480
exceeded 5,000.

404
23:50.800 --> 23:52.330
The 3rd Red Army Corps alone

405
23:52.480 --> 23:56.240
lost over 2,700 men.

406
23:56.470 --> 23:59.630
Comrade Li De, tell me,

407
24:00.030 --> 24:01.200
when will you

408
24:01.790 --> 24:05.310
stop insisting on this mistaken strategy?

409
24:05.670 --> 24:08.520
...stop insisting on this mistaken strategy?

410
24:08.830 --> 24:10.030
Comrade Bo Gu,

411
24:10.110 --> 24:11.710
next time you make my coffee,

412
24:12.070 --> 24:13.530
don't use water like this.

413
24:16.600 --> 24:17.810
Okay, Comrade Li De.

414
24:18.450 --> 24:19.580
That was my mistake.

415
24:22.930 --> 24:25.330
Comrade Li De, thank you for your hard work.

416
24:27.630 --> 24:28.490
Comrade Luofu.

417
24:28.510 --> 24:29.130
Comrade Li De

418
24:29.130 --> 24:32.200
is a military adviser sent by the Communist International.

419
24:32.200 --> 24:33.510
To some extent,

420
24:33.660 --> 24:35.140
he represents the Communist International.

421
24:35.140 --> 24:36.990
We accept the leadership of the Communist International.

422
24:36.990 --> 24:37.840
Is that wrong?

423
24:39.660 --> 24:42.080
Accepting its leadership

424
24:42.290 --> 24:44.510
doesn't mean blindly following one person

425
24:44.510 --> 24:47.320
and agreeing with everything he says.

426
24:49.170 --> 24:51.080
I don't understand your insinuations

427
24:51.080 --> 24:52.160
or what you're implying.

428
24:52.160 --> 24:53.920
Stay out of military

429
24:54.120 --> 24:55.250
command decisions.

430
24:55.950 --> 24:58.300
Then I'll put it in terms you can understand.

431
24:58.300 --> 25:01.610
I'm a secretary of the Central Secretariat.

432
25:02.160 --> 25:04.830
I can't stand by and watch our Red Army

433
25:05.000 --> 25:08.070
be wiped out fighting the enemy head-on.

434
25:08.110 --> 25:10.350
Who wants to see our forces wiped out?

435
25:10.800 --> 25:12.400
This is an opportunistic way of thinking.

436
25:12.400 --> 25:13.290
Plekhanov

437
25:13.310 --> 25:16.310
opposed an armed uprising in Russia in 1905.

438
25:16.370 --> 25:17.660
He was taking the same position as you back then.

439
25:17.660 --> 25:21.330
Plekhanov was completely opposed to armed uprisings.

440
25:21.710 --> 25:24.650
I'm saying we can't rely solely on defense,

441
25:24.680 --> 25:26.050
holding positions at all costs and fighting head-on.

442
25:26.050 --> 25:29.240
We must find other ways to defeat the enemy.

443
25:29.570 --> 25:31.940
What do those two positions have in common?

444
25:31.940 --> 25:34.730
And when it comes to the history of the revolutions in Soviet Russia,

445
25:34.730 --> 25:37.580
I have more right to speak than you do.

446
25:37.670 --> 25:38.900
You don't have to remind me of that.

447
25:38.900 --> 25:39.960
You're a celebrated Marxist scholar

448
25:39.960 --> 25:41.850
from Moscow Sun Yat-sen University.

449
25:41.850 --> 25:43.020
When it comes to theory,

450
25:43.020 --> 25:45.400
even Comrade Wang Ming holds you in high regard.

451
25:45.400 --> 25:46.510
But let me remind you,

452
25:46.510 --> 25:48.610
you're not a member of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission.

453
25:48.610 --> 25:51.060
You have no say in military command.

454
25:51.250 --> 25:54.550
This concerns the very survival of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army.

455
25:54.550 --> 25:55.980
Of course I have a say!

456
25:56.380 --> 25:58.380
Our affairs here in China

457
25:58.700 --> 26:00.630
cannot depend entirely on Li De.

458
26:00.720 --> 26:02.480
We must think for ourselves.

459
26:02.680 --> 26:05.310
Otherwise, if we keep fighting this way,

460
26:05.510 --> 26:08.770
the 5th Counter-Encirclement Campaign is doomed to fail!

461
26:08.960 --> 26:09.940
What kind of attitude is that?

462
26:09.940 --> 26:11.310
A realistic one!

463
26:32.020 --> 26:33.630
We should review the lessons

464
26:35.280 --> 26:36.680
of the Battle of Guangchang,

465
26:36.680 --> 26:37.680
but not right now.

466
26:38.160 --> 26:39.160
Our most urgent task

467
26:39.160 --> 26:41.920
is to come up with a plan for our next move.

468
26:42.070 --> 26:44.390
Comrades Bo Gu and Luofu,

469
26:45.580 --> 26:47.170
do you agree?

470
27:04.870 --> 27:07.870
Comrade Bo Gu, please continue.

471
27:17.090 --> 27:19.450
After much deliberation, Comrade Li De and I

472
27:19.450 --> 27:21.400
have both concluded that it will be extremely difficult

473
27:21.400 --> 27:23.670
to break the enemy's encirclement

474
27:24.050 --> 27:25.670
within the Central Soviet Area.

475
27:25.670 --> 27:28.310
We should break out decisively and move beyond our lines,

476
27:28.310 --> 27:30.790
securing a much larger area in which to fight

477
27:31.070 --> 27:32.750
and turning the tables on the enemy

478
27:32.750 --> 27:34.790
to break their encirclement.

479
27:34.920 --> 27:36.810
Didn't Comrade Mao Zedong

480
27:37.050 --> 27:38.810
propose this very strategy

481
27:38.900 --> 27:40.680
for breaking the encirclement before?

482
27:40.680 --> 27:42.110
Times have changed.

483
27:42.130 --> 27:45.200
When Mao Zedong proposed it, the situation wasn't right.

484
27:45.200 --> 27:47.110
Now that Comrade Li De has proposed it,

485
27:47.110 --> 27:48.840
the timing couldn't be better.

486
27:51.510 --> 27:54.090
Of course, these are only our preliminary ideas.

487
27:54.090 --> 27:55.960
The final plan

488
27:56.230 --> 27:58.570
will have to await approval from the Communist International.

489
27:58.570 --> 28:00.630
Do we have any concrete measures yet?

490
28:02.530 --> 28:03.530
Not at the moment.

491
28:06.310 --> 28:08.440
As for a specific operational plan...

492
28:09.710 --> 28:12.640
I believe we need to convene

493
28:12.670 --> 28:13.930
an enlarged meeting of the Political Bureau

494
28:13.930 --> 28:17.260
to study the matter, discuss it, and hear everyone's views.

495
28:18.740 --> 28:19.650
Comrade Enlai,

496
28:19.720 --> 28:21.610
until we receive

497
28:21.640 --> 28:23.830
clear instructions from the Communist International,

498
28:23.830 --> 28:25.440
we shouldn't involve more people in this.

499
28:25.440 --> 28:28.040
It would be unwise to cause unnecessary alarm.

500
28:28.310 --> 28:29.240
I suggest

501
28:29.340 --> 28:32.210
that Comrade Li De be put in charge of drafting

502
28:32.320 --> 28:33.550
a strategic relocation plan

503
28:33.550 --> 28:37.150
and submitting it to the Communist International for approval.

504
28:37.620 --> 28:39.280
I hereby adjourn the meeting.

505
29:01.550 --> 29:02.760
Comrade Bo Gu.

506
29:04.800 --> 29:06.870
You were unwise just now.

507
29:07.610 --> 29:10.960
You and Luofu both studied in the Soviet Union.

508
29:10.990 --> 29:11.970
The Chinese Revolution

509
29:11.970 --> 29:18.300
should be led by those who returned from Moscow.

510
29:18.330 --> 29:21.280
You need him now.

511
29:24.300 --> 29:25.540
Comrade Li De,

512
29:26.440 --> 29:30.360
I deeply admire your magnanimity.

513
29:30.730 --> 29:31.940
Thank you, Bo Gu.

514
29:34.240 --> 29:35.290
Comrade Xiuquan,

515
29:35.680 --> 29:38.050
please deal with the water issue first.

516
29:39.400 --> 29:40.210
All right.

517
29:42.920 --> 29:47.090
But working with Luofu has become nearly impossible.

518
29:47.120 --> 29:49.840
He's growing more and more distant from us,

519
29:50.000 --> 29:52.400
while drawing closer to Mao Zedong.

520
29:52.470 --> 29:57.710
He's caught the disease of right opportunism.

521
29:59.290 --> 30:00.530
Where is Mao now?

522
30:00.920 --> 30:03.670
He's gone to Huichang.

523
30:05.700 --> 30:06.790
Huichang?

524
30:06.820 --> 30:07.320
Yes.

525
30:08.310 --> 30:09.470
I've heard

526
30:09.610 --> 30:16.780
he held a meeting of Guangdong-Jiangxi Provincial cadres in Huichang

527
30:17.140 --> 30:21.340
to learn the situation on the southern front,

528
30:22.570 --> 30:26.060
build local armed forces to wage guerrilla warfare,

529
30:26.120 --> 30:32.360
resume tungsten mining,

530
30:32.790 --> 30:36.310
and restore trade with areas under Nationalist control.

531
30:36.310 --> 30:39.600
In short, it's all the same old ideas.

532
30:39.620 --> 30:41.140
What a stubborn man.

533
30:41.170 --> 30:41.970
That's right.

534
30:44.270 --> 30:45.000
Bo Gu,

535
30:45.930 --> 30:47.850
weren't you going to send him to Moscow?

536
30:47.850 --> 30:49.810
Comrade Wang Ming has already replied by telegram.

537
30:49.810 --> 30:51.940
Citing safety concerns along the way,

538
30:52.500 --> 30:55.410
he opposed sending Mao Zedong to Moscow.

539
30:58.730 --> 31:01.940
[Wenwuba, Huichang, Jiangxi]

540
31:01.940 --> 31:05.150
[Headquarters of the Guangdong-Jiangxi Provincial Committee of the CPC]

541
31:06.750 --> 31:07.750
Chairman Mao.

542
31:11.220 --> 31:14.310
Changgong, how is the fighting on the southern front?

543
31:17.800 --> 31:20.520
Chairman, things are going very well.

544
31:20.850 --> 31:21.850
The 22nd Red Army Division,

545
31:21.850 --> 31:23.440
following your earlier instructions,

546
31:23.440 --> 31:25.870
has won several battles using guerrilla tactics

547
31:25.870 --> 31:28.030
between Junmenling and Huichang.

548
31:28.510 --> 31:29.570
Now the Guangdong Army

549
31:29.570 --> 31:31.610
has retreated into its blockhouses at Junmenling again,

550
31:31.610 --> 31:32.740
and is staying put.

551
31:32.850 --> 31:33.850
Just as expected.

552
31:34.200 --> 31:35.290
Chen Jitang

553
31:35.920 --> 31:37.640
isn't all that determined

554
31:37.690 --> 31:39.020
to attack our base area.

555
31:39.240 --> 31:42.300
With the 22nd Red Army Division keeping them occupied,

556
31:42.480 --> 31:43.440
Huichang

557
31:44.020 --> 31:46.280
should remain relatively quiet for now.

558
31:50.090 --> 31:52.090
But, Chairman,

559
31:52.120 --> 31:54.810
the troops are in high spirits.

560
31:55.000 --> 31:57.580
Yet the Central Revolutionary Military Commission has sent a work team

561
31:57.580 --> 31:59.810
to investigate the alleged right-deviationist errors

562
31:59.810 --> 32:01.240
of losing Junmenling.

563
32:01.310 --> 32:03.630
Deputy Political Commissar Fang Qiang has been dismissed

564
32:03.630 --> 32:07.030
and taken to the Security Bureau for further investigation.

565
32:10.520 --> 32:11.580
Just as I expected.

566
32:13.960 --> 32:16.270
Who has taken over as political commissar of the 22nd Red Army Division?

567
32:16.270 --> 32:19.050
It's Huang Kaixiang, formerly of the 10th Red Army in northeastern Jiangxi.

568
32:19.050 --> 32:20.000
Huang Kaixiang?

569
32:21.910 --> 32:23.070
I've heard of him.

570
32:23.880 --> 32:25.410
He's Fang Zhimin's cousin,

571
32:25.510 --> 32:27.340
a fierce warrior with both brains and brawn.

572
32:27.340 --> 32:28.230
Chairman,

573
32:28.370 --> 32:30.230
Huang Kaixiang was eager to meet you

574
32:30.230 --> 32:32.050
after hearing you were in Wenwuba.

575
32:32.050 --> 32:33.310
He's right over there.

576
32:36.060 --> 32:36.940
I'll go get him.

577
32:36.970 --> 32:37.480
No need.

578
32:45.250 --> 32:47.050
Are you Comrade Huang Kaixiang?

579
32:49.290 --> 32:51.400
Chairman Mao, I am Huang Kaixiang.

580
32:51.800 --> 32:53.350
You're the axe-wielding general like Cheng Yaojin

581
32:53.350 --> 32:55.950
whom Enlai often talks about, aren't you?

582
32:55.520 --> 32:59.570
[Huang Kaixiang, Political Commissar of the 22nd Red Army Division]

583
32:57.440 --> 32:58.410
Chairman Mao,

584
32:58.570 --> 33:00.900
I'm nowhere near as brave as Cheng Yaojin.

585
33:01.320 --> 33:03.230
You followed Fang Zhimin in the revolution,

586
33:03.230 --> 33:04.860
and Enlai speaks highly of you to this day.

587
33:04.860 --> 33:06.000
I'd say you're even better

588
33:06.000 --> 33:07.480
than Cheng Yaojin.

589
33:08.310 --> 33:10.480
I've heard you have 3 treasures.

590
33:10.750 --> 33:12.110
May I have a look at them?

591
33:12.300 --> 33:13.700
Of course, Chairman Mao.

592
33:14.560 --> 33:16.030
Here's the first one.

593
33:16.300 --> 33:18.490
As you can see, it's this pocket watch.

594
33:18.780 --> 33:21.510
During the 4th Counter-Encirclement Campaign,

595
33:21.640 --> 33:22.900
when I led the 82nd Regiment

596
33:22.900 --> 33:24.580
in combat in the Central Soviet Area,

597
33:24.580 --> 33:26.380
Vice Chairman Zhou gave it to me.

598
33:27.810 --> 33:28.610
The second one

599
33:29.240 --> 33:30.310
is this pistol.

600
33:31.370 --> 33:32.920
When Commander-in-Chief Zhu

601
33:32.920 --> 33:34.550
saw me fighting the enemy with an axe,

602
33:34.550 --> 33:36.950
he took his own sidearm off and gave it to me.

603
33:37.440 --> 33:39.200
And the third one is

604
33:40.720 --> 33:41.790
this axe of mine.

605
33:43.850 --> 33:44.820
Comrade Kaixiang.

606
33:44.820 --> 33:45.350
Yes, sir.

607
33:45.640 --> 33:48.360
I have nothing else to give you,

608
33:48.570 --> 33:50.430
so I'll leave you with some words:

609
33:50.600 --> 33:53.950
Stay mobile and flexible. Destroy the enemy on the move.

610
33:55.110 --> 33:57.750
Stay mobile and flexible. Destroy the enemy on the move.

611
33:57.750 --> 33:59.950
Yes, Chairman Mao. I'll remember that.

612
33:59.960 --> 34:01.270
As long as they help me win battles, that's all that matters.

613
34:01.270 --> 34:02.000
Chairman.

614
34:03.680 --> 34:04.940
Reporting, Chairman.

615
34:06.200 --> 34:09.000
Chairman, Vice Chairman Zhou has sent a telegram.

616
34:11.760 --> 34:13.010
He asks you to return to Ruijin immediately

617
34:13.010 --> 34:16.070
to attend an enlarged meeting of the Political Bureau.

618
34:18.330 --> 34:21.270
[Shazhouba, Ruijin, Jiangxi]

619
34:18.920 --> 34:21.510
On June 16, 1934,

620
34:21.270 --> 34:24.219
[Office of the CPC Central Committee]

621
34:21.960 --> 34:24.440
the Communist International sent a reply to the Central Committee of the CPC

622
34:24.440 --> 34:26.570
regarding the strategic relocation.

623
34:26.610 --> 34:29.139
It agreed with the strategic relocation plan

624
34:29.210 --> 34:31.070
previously proposed by the Central Committee.

625
34:31.070 --> 34:32.400
However, it also stated

626
34:32.590 --> 34:35.429
that the Central Soviet Area's resources were not yet exhausted,

627
34:35.429 --> 34:37.489
and that the Red Army's combat forces

628
34:37.610 --> 34:38.960
and sentiment in the rear

629
34:38.960 --> 34:41.330
had not yet become cause for concern.

630
34:42.000 --> 34:44.070
This led Bo Gu and Li De

631
34:44.070 --> 34:46.760
to slow down preparations for the strategic relocation.

632
34:46.760 --> 34:48.630
Comrades,

633
34:48.750 --> 34:50.980
everyone should share their views.

634
34:51.550 --> 34:53.210
I've called you all here today

635
34:53.800 --> 34:54.760
to discuss

636
34:54.780 --> 34:56.639
our course of action from here on.

637
34:57.110 --> 34:58.510
Everyone present

638
34:58.620 --> 35:01.100
holds an important leadership position.

639
35:01.400 --> 35:02.530
So I hope you will all

640
35:02.760 --> 35:03.760
speak freely

641
35:04.440 --> 35:05.910
and share your thoughts.

642
35:13.020 --> 35:13.980
Comrade Zedong,

643
35:14.760 --> 35:15.910
if you have any ideas,

644
35:15.910 --> 35:17.770
please share them with everyone.

645
35:23.580 --> 35:24.940
Today's meeting

646
35:25.300 --> 35:28.140
isn't going the way I expected.

647
35:28.660 --> 35:29.660
I thought

648
35:29.840 --> 35:32.800
the Central Committee had called this urgent meeting

649
35:32.800 --> 35:35.670
to announce its plan for our next move

650
35:35.690 --> 35:37.290
and let everyone discuss it.

651
35:37.590 --> 35:39.000
What is meant by "the Central Committee"?

652
35:39.000 --> 35:41.230
The Central Committee is the brain of the whole Party.

653
35:41.230 --> 35:42.830
It should always plan ahead.

654
35:43.350 --> 35:44.480
Comrade Mao Zedong,

655
35:44.840 --> 35:47.960
whether the Central Committee has a plan is its own business.

656
35:47.960 --> 35:49.440
Why are you pressing so hard?

657
35:49.440 --> 35:51.240
I'm not the one pressing so hard.

658
35:51.480 --> 35:52.230
It's Chiang Kai-shek

659
35:52.230 --> 35:53.820
and his Nationalist army who are pressing us so hard.

660
35:53.820 --> 35:54.780
Comrade Zedong,

661
35:55.560 --> 35:57.850
we'd like to hear your thoughts.

662
35:59.880 --> 36:00.720
My thoughts

663
36:01.720 --> 36:04.070
have been presented to the Central Committee many times.

664
36:04.070 --> 36:05.130
It's quite simple.

665
36:06.560 --> 36:09.440
With the enemy's massive forces closing in,

666
36:10.130 --> 36:12.450
the Central Soviet Area's strategic space

667
36:12.450 --> 36:13.450
has been completely squeezed out,

668
36:13.450 --> 36:14.920
and our efforts to fight on interior lines

669
36:14.920 --> 36:17.250
can no longer turn the situation around.

670
36:17.550 --> 36:20.750
The Central Committee should act quickly and decisively

671
36:20.820 --> 36:23.330
to move the surviving forces of the Central Red Army

672
36:23.330 --> 36:24.440
beyond our lines,

673
36:24.850 --> 36:26.410
use mobile warfare

674
36:26.470 --> 36:27.970
to keep the enemy on the move,

675
36:27.970 --> 36:29.280
look for opportunities to strike,

676
36:29.280 --> 36:32.010
and ultimately break the enemy's encirclement.

677
36:35.480 --> 36:36.940
Does anyone have any thoughts

678
36:36.940 --> 36:38.870
on Comrade Mao Zedong's proposal?

679
36:40.260 --> 36:43.340
I think Mao has a point.

680
36:43.770 --> 36:46.460
Chiang Kai-shek is following Zeng Guofan's example,

681
36:46.460 --> 36:49.500
using fortified camps and a slow, grinding approach

682
36:49.850 --> 36:50.770
to deal with us.

683
36:51.060 --> 36:52.260
And what are we doing?

684
36:52.800 --> 36:54.950
Instead of waging mobile warfare,

685
36:55.340 --> 36:56.700
we're copying their tactics,

686
36:56.700 --> 36:58.450
using fortified camps and a slow, grinding approach,

687
36:58.450 --> 37:00.910
keeping our troops pinned down in one place.

688
37:02.170 --> 37:03.130
Chiang Kai-shek

689
37:04.490 --> 37:05.610
must be delighted.

690
37:06.480 --> 37:07.680
Experience has shown

691
37:07.800 --> 37:09.730
that Comrade Mao Zedong's tactics

692
37:09.770 --> 37:11.950
proved effective in the previous

693
37:12.900 --> 37:14.900
counter-encirclement campaigns.

694
37:15.070 --> 37:16.400
It's easy for you to say.

695
37:17.000 --> 37:18.710
Are we just supposed to abandon

696
37:18.710 --> 37:21.070
the vast Central Soviet Area and the base areas we fought for

697
37:21.070 --> 37:22.130
over so many years?

698
37:22.230 --> 37:23.310
What's the alternative?

699
37:23.310 --> 37:24.860
Stay in the base area and wait to die?

700
37:24.860 --> 37:25.770
[Xiang Ying, Member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee,]

701
37:25.280 --> 37:26.760
And how do we justify that politically?

702
37:25.770 --> 37:26.680
[Vice Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

703
37:27.030 --> 37:28.000
If we're wiped out by the encirclement,

704
37:28.000 --> 37:29.920
we'll be able to justify that politically?

705
37:29.920 --> 37:32.780
Fine. Then let's hear from you, Comrade Mao Zedong.

706
37:33.590 --> 37:35.300
How exactly do you propose we relocate?

707
37:35.300 --> 37:36.440
Where do we intend to go?

708
37:36.440 --> 37:38.970
And how exactly will you wage mobile warfare?

709
37:43.070 --> 37:45.270
Given the enemy's current deployment,

710
37:45.560 --> 37:48.150
moving northeast is no longer a viable option.

711
37:48.150 --> 37:49.590
Our only choice is to head west.

712
37:49.590 --> 37:50.790
We must break through

713
37:50.800 --> 37:53.400
a weak point in the enemy's fortified defenses

714
37:53.420 --> 37:55.200
[Chen Yun, Member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee]

715
37:53.710 --> 37:55.550
and advance into central Hunan.

716
37:55.650 --> 37:57.400
We can draw the enemy forces in Jiangxi

717
37:57.400 --> 37:58.660
toward central Hunan,

718
37:58.760 --> 38:00.930
then look for opportunities to strike on the move

719
38:00.930 --> 38:02.030
and destroy the enemy.

720
38:02.030 --> 38:03.470
After that, we turn east

721
38:03.500 --> 38:06.760
and return to the Central Soviet Area in southern Jiangxi.

722
38:08.040 --> 38:08.770
Mao,

723
38:09.400 --> 38:12.320
your idea is absurdly naive.

724
38:16.930 --> 38:18.740
Your idea is absurdly naive.

725
38:18.990 --> 38:22.840
Do you think Chiang Kai-shek's hundreds of thousands of troops

726
38:23.160 --> 38:27.160
will move at your command like puppets on strings?

727
38:27.690 --> 38:29.210
If we break out west,

728
38:29.540 --> 38:32.310
our forces will be severely outnumbered.

729
38:32.360 --> 38:34.190
How will we reinforce them?

730
38:34.630 --> 38:37.290
And what about food, weapons,

731
38:37.320 --> 38:38.590
and ammunition?

732
38:40.240 --> 38:41.960
Translate what I'm about to say.

733
38:41.960 --> 38:43.320
Tell him I'd like to hear

734
38:43.550 --> 38:45.480
what he, the military adviser, has to say.

735
38:45.480 --> 38:46.840
I'd like to hear

736
38:46.860 --> 38:49.130
what your plan is.

737
38:49.150 --> 38:50.930
[Liu Shaoqi, Alternate Member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee]

738
38:49.580 --> 38:52.950
My position is clear.

739
38:53.230 --> 38:55.360
Our current forces

740
38:55.550 --> 38:57.880
are strong enough to fight the enemy in a final decisive battle

741
38:57.880 --> 39:00.550
within the Central Soviet Area.

742
39:00.550 --> 39:01.590
Our current forces

743
39:01.590 --> 39:03.070
are strong enough to fight the enemy in a final decisive battle

744
39:03.070 --> 39:04.870
within the Central Soviet Area.

745
39:05.060 --> 39:08.270
The Central Soviet Area has been squeezed to its limits.

746
39:08.290 --> 39:09.800
How much strategic room do we have left?

747
39:09.800 --> 39:11.070
How much strategic room do we have left?

748
39:11.070 --> 39:12.270
The enemy is right in front of us.

749
39:12.270 --> 39:13.210
Hesitate when decisive action is needed...

750
39:13.210 --> 39:14.110
The enemy is right in front of us.

751
39:14.110 --> 39:17.910
Hesitate when decisive action is needed, and we'll miss our chance!

752
39:18.250 --> 39:18.910
Translate!

753
39:19.960 --> 39:22.670
This is our last chance.

754
39:23.320 --> 39:25.270
You're afraid of the enemy.

755
39:25.290 --> 39:28.490
The Red Army will never retreat under any circumstances.

756
39:29.740 --> 39:31.290
You're afraid to face the enemy and fight.

757
39:31.290 --> 39:31.960
The Central Red Army

758
39:31.960 --> 39:34.070
will never retreat or flee lightly.

759
39:34.180 --> 39:36.050
I agree with Comrade Li De.

760
39:36.610 --> 39:38.820
Breaking out with our main force into Hunan

761
39:38.820 --> 39:40.550
would be extremely difficult.

762
39:40.560 --> 39:43.480
Besides, the Central Committee has never proposed

763
39:43.810 --> 39:45.270
a full-scale relocation.

764
39:50.850 --> 39:52.310
I have nothing more to say.

765
39:53.180 --> 39:56.540
All right, let's continue the meeting.

766
40:09.630 --> 40:10.630
I now announce

767
40:11.710 --> 40:12.510
two

768
40:13.200 --> 40:16.390
action plans approved by the Communist International.

769
40:16.650 --> 40:17.400
First,

770
40:17.590 --> 40:20.250
we have decided to send out the 7th Red Army Corps

771
40:20.260 --> 40:22.610
to form the Northern Expeditionary Advance Team Against Japan.

772
40:22.610 --> 40:24.630
It will advance north

773
40:24.630 --> 40:27.140
into the border regions of Fujian, Zhejiang, Jiangxi, and Anhui,

774
40:27.140 --> 40:28.740
establish guerrilla zones,

775
40:28.740 --> 40:31.080
and seek opportunities to set up base areas.

776
40:31.080 --> 40:33.000
The goal is to draw away enemy forces

777
40:33.000 --> 40:36.110
and ease the military pressure on the Central Soviet Area.

778
40:36.110 --> 40:36.840
Second,

779
40:36.860 --> 40:38.140
we have decided to reorganize the Red Army forces

780
40:38.140 --> 40:40.000
in the Hunan-Jiangxi Soviet Area

781
40:40.280 --> 40:41.740
into the 6th Red Army Corps

782
40:42.110 --> 40:44.670
and break through the encirclement to move into central Hunan.

783
40:44.670 --> 40:48.670
There, they will seek an opportunity to establish reliable contact

784
40:48.900 --> 40:50.630
with He Long's 3rd Red Army in western Hunan and Hubei.

785
40:50.630 --> 40:52.130
If no one has any objections

786
40:52.130 --> 40:54.090
to these two plans,

787
40:54.280 --> 40:56.880
we'll put them into action as soon as possible.

788
40:59.680 --> 41:00.480
Comrades,

789
41:00.890 --> 41:02.820
to better formulate and implement

790
41:02.960 --> 41:05.200
our new strategy for breaking the enemy's encirclement,

791
41:05.200 --> 41:06.420
the Central Committee has decided

792
41:06.420 --> 41:09.790
that Comrade Li De, Comrade Zhou Enlai, and I

793
41:09.810 --> 41:11.710
will take charge of the command together.

794
41:11.710 --> 41:13.070
I will assume overall responsibility.

795
41:13.070 --> 41:16.110
Comrade Li De will formulate the military strategy.

796
41:16.670 --> 41:17.730
Comrade Zhou Enlai

797
41:17.960 --> 41:19.840
will oversee its implementation.

798
41:19.840 --> 41:20.800
All plans

799
41:21.150 --> 41:22.760
are top military secrets.

800
41:23.070 --> 41:24.600
No one else is to interfere.

801
41:25.000 --> 41:27.800
You will simply follow orders when the time comes.

802
41:30.320 --> 41:31.240
Comrades,

803
41:31.670 --> 41:33.730
this is a matter of military discipline.

804
41:33.730 --> 41:35.390
It must be strictly observed.

805
41:45.760 --> 41:46.890
Meeting adjourned.

806
42:24.250 --> 42:25.580
-Comrade Zedong. -Mao.

807
42:30.810 --> 42:31.740
Comrade Zedong,

808
42:32.590 --> 42:34.320
I'd like to explain something.

809
42:34.320 --> 42:37.230
The 7th Red Army Corps is heading north to divert the enemy.

810
42:37.230 --> 42:40.280
The 6th Red Army Corps is moving west to scout the way.

811
42:44.030 --> 42:46.840
Is there some grand strategic plan behind all this

812
42:48.250 --> 42:49.980
that you can't openly discuss?

813
42:52.130 --> 42:54.440
We'll have to see how the situation develops.

814
42:54.440 --> 42:56.070
It should become clear before long.

815
42:56.070 --> 42:57.530
Please tell Comrade Bo Gu:

816
42:57.600 --> 43:00.440
Once the plan is laid, it's time to make a decision.

817
43:00.840 --> 43:03.720
A lack of resolve will lead to utter defeat.
